<%#
  /verification — §6.10: “the trust page: explains the three grades, the
  HonestCars Checklist, photo examples of catches (flood, odometer), integrity
  rules (‘inspectors never take seller money’). Most underrated page on the
  site — give it design love.”
%>
<section class="trust-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <%- include('../partials/breadcrumbs', { crumbs: trail }) %>
    <p class="eyebrow">Verification</p>
    <h1>Every grade is a promise about how much we actually know</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      There is no “we think it is fine” grade. Each listing carries exactly one of three labels, and
      each label says precisely what has been checked — and what has not.
    </p>
    <div class="stat-band mt-3">
      <div class="stat"><span class="stat__value"><%= counters.carsLive %></span><span class="stat__label">cars in the network today</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="stat__value"><%= counters.certified %></span><span class="stat__label">HonestCars-Certified</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="stat__value"><%= counters.partnerDealers %></span><span class="stat__label">verified partner lots</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="stat__value"><%= counters.carsSold90d %></span><span class="stat__label">deals closed in 90 days</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>The three grades</h2>
      <p class="section-head__note mb-0">Admin-set, visible on every card and every VDP. No grade is ever upgraded without a new inspection.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grade-deep">
      <article class="grade-deep__card grade-deep__card--network_listed">
        <div class="row row--between">
          <h3 class="mb-0">● Network-Listed</h3>
          <span class="badge badge--network_listed">Dealer data only</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mb-0">
          A partner dealer supplied the details and the photos. We have not stood next to the car. Useful for
          price range and availability — and honestly labelled so you never assume more than that.
        </p>
        <ul class="tick-list">
          <li class="tick-list__yes"><%- helpers.icon('check', { size: 16 }) %> <span>VIN-level data recorded (ops side), asking price and location verified with the dealer</span></li>
          <li class="tick-list__no"><%- helpers.icon('close', { size: 16 }) %> <span>No physical inspection, no OBD2 scan, no documents sighted</span></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="grade-deep__meta mb-0">Best for: narrowing a shortlist. Not enough to pay on.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="grade-deep__card grade-deep__card--field_checked">
        <div class="row row--between">
          <h3 class="mb-0">● Field-Checked</h3>
          <span class="badge badge--field_checked">Inspector on site</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mb-0">
          One of our inspectors physically visited the car, photographed it where it stands and confirmed the
          basics. It is more than a listing — it is not yet a full report.
        </p>
        <ul class="tick-list">
          <li class="tick-list__yes"><%- helpers.icon('check', { size: 16 }) %> <span>Exterior and interior photos taken by us, on site, on the day</span></li>
          <li class="tick-list__yes"><%- helpers.icon('check', { size: 16 }) %> <span>Mileage, panel condition and obvious faults recorded</span></li>
          <li class="tick-list__no"><%- helpers.icon('close', { size: 16 }) %> <span>No road test or full mechanical checklist unless a report is attached</span></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="grade-deep__meta mb-0">Best for: deciding whether the car is worth a full inspection.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="grade-deep__card grade-deep__card--certified">
        <div class="row row--between">
          <h3 class="mb-0">● HonestCars-Certified</h3>
          <span class="badge badge--certified">Full checklist passed</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mb-0">
          The whole checklist was run: OBD2 scan, documents sighted at source, body read for repair, road test,
          and an honest note written for a buyer. The report is attached to the listing.
        </p>
        <ul class="tick-list">
          <li class="tick-list__yes"><%- helpers.icon('check', { size: 16 }) %> <span>Ten-point checklist with photos of every finding</span></li>
          <li class="tick-list__yes"><%- helpers.icon('check', { size: 16 }) %> <span>Documents sighted at the source, not photocopies</span></li>
          <li class="tick-list__yes"><%- helpers.icon('check', { size: 16 }) %> <span>Honest note: what made us hesitate, written plainly</span></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="grade-deep__meta mb-0">Best for: buying remotely, or when you cannot bring a mechanic.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--surface">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>The HonestCars Checklist</h2>
      <p class="section-head__note mb-0">Ten things, every certified car. The report shows which line produced which finding.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="checklist-grid">
      <% checklist.forEach(function (item) { %>
        <div class="checklist-grid__item">
          <%- helpers.icon('checkCircle', { size: 18 }) %>
          <span><%= item %></span>
        </div>
      <% }); %>
    </div>
    <p class="page-hero__meta mt-3">
      What we do not do: open engines or gearboxes, or certify structural repairs without a workshop report.
      When a car needs that, we say so and point you at the right specialist — see the
      <a href="/services/inspection">inspection page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>What we actually catch</h2>
      <p class="section-head__note mb-0">Three real examples, with the finding that changed the deal.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid--3">
      <% catches.forEach(function (item) { %>
        <article class="catch-card">
          <% var catchBlur = helpers.blurFor(item.image); %>
          <div class="catch-card__media media-blur"<% if (catchBlur) { %> style="background-image:url('<%= catchBlur %>')"<% } %>>
            <img data-blur-img src="<%= helpers.photoSrc(item.image) %>" alt="<%= helpers.esc(item.title) %> — illustrative condition photo"
                 <% if (helpers.srcsetFor(item.image)) { %>srcset="<%= helpers.srcsetFor(item.image) %>" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 380px, 92vw"<% } %>
                 width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          </div>
          <span class="catch-card__tag"><%= item.tag %></span>
          <h3 class="mb-0"><%= item.title %></h3>
          <p class="mb-0"><%= item.copy %></p>
        </article>
      <% }); %>
    </div>
    <p class="field__hint mt-2">
      Illustrative photography. On the live site each catch links to the actual listing photos with the
      fault circled.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="integrity-band">
      <h2>Integrity rules we work under</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Inspectors never take money from sellers.</strong> Not for a good report, not for a fast one. It is a dismissable offence and we audit it.</li>
        <li><strong>We write what we find, including the faults that cost us the sale.</strong> A listed car with a fault note is worth more to us than a silent problem.</li>
        <li><strong>Buyer money never goes to the seller directly.</strong> Protected channels only, every time.</li>
        <li><strong>Grades are earned, not sold.</strong> Dealers cannot buy a Certified badge, and featured placement never changes a grade.</li>
        <li><strong>If we are wrong, we correct it in writing</strong> — and we show you the corrected report.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<% if (examples.length) { %>
<section class="section section--surface">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Certified cars you can look at today</h2>
      <a class="section-head__link" href="/cars?grade=certified">All certified cars →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid--3">
      <% examples.forEach(function (listing) { %>
        <%- include('../partials/car-card', { listing: listing, helpers: helpers }) %>
      <% }); %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<% } %>

<% if (testimonials.length) { %>
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head"><h2>From buyers who were told the truth</h2></div>
    <div class="grid grid--2">
      <% testimonials.forEach(function (testimonial) { %>
        <figure class="testimonial">
          <span class="testimonial__stars" aria-label="<%= testimonial.rating %> out of 5">★★★★★</span>
          <blockquote class="testimonial__quote">“<%= testimonial.quote %>”</blockquote>
          <figcaption class="testimonial__meta"><%= testimonial.name %> · <%= testimonial.area %></figcaption>
        </figure>
      <% }); %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<% } %>

<% if (faqs.length) { %>
<section class="section section--surface">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Verification questions</h2></div>
    <%- include('../partials/accordion', { faqs: faqs, idPrefix: 'verification-faq' }) %>
  </div>
</section>
<% } %>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="cta-band">
      <div>
        <h2>Want this run on a car you found somewhere else?</h2>
        <p class="mb-0">Send us the location. An inspector goes, scans and writes the report — usually the same day.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/services/inspection">Book an inspection</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="<%= site.nav.whatsapp.general %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
           data-event="whatsapp_click" data-source="verification">Ask a question first</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
